  "caption": "Quinn got a knee scan report with the words 'meniscus tear' and spent the evening reading worst-case forum posts.\n\nIn middle age, meniscus changes are really common, including in knees that don't hurt at all. A scan is only part of the story, and for these wear-related tears, exercise is usually the first step.\n\nWhat often helps: steady strength work for the quads, hips and calves over about three months, getting comfortable bending and straightening back, and a gradual return to walking, stairs and sport. In a flare-up, trim the dose rather than stopping completely.\n\nIf your knee truly locks or gets stuck, or a sudden twist brings swelling, get it checked early.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
